# Invariant = test (process rule)

Pattern from review rounds 3–6: a docstring/doc promises a mechanic, the code
implements a simplification, review finds the gap. From now on:

**Every protocol invariant ships with a test in the same commit. An invariant
without a test does not exist.**

Current mapping (keep updated):

| Invariant | Test |
|---|---|
| Aliases per deliberation, 27+ models | tests/test_anonymize.py |
| 429 transient vs quota, 4xx fail-fast | tests/test_openrouter.py |
| Budget per question (delta), pre-call estimate | tests/test_openrouter.py |
| Revision converges platforms (not attrition) | tests/test_e2e.py::test_debate_loop_with_platform_revision |
| Stability rule blocks a flip | tests/test_e2e.py::test_stability_rule_blocks_a_flip |
| Smart mode without callback degrades, never drops | tests/test_e2e.py::test_smart_mode_without_callback_degrades |
| Switch needs open objection + cited argument | tests/test_debate.py |
| Closure only by target faction; supersede leaves ledger | tests/test_debate.py |
| CLI imports without factions↔judges cycle | tests/test_imports.py |
| CLI --auto-clarify / --no-clarify flags | tests/test_cli.py |
| Nearest .env up to git root, no override | tests/test_env.py |
| Progress callback optional; stages emitted | tests/test_e2e.py::test_progress_emits_protocol_stages |
| Near-duplicate primary rec merges; negation never auto-merges | tests/test_factions.py |
| UNANIMOUS ⇒ no minority; deadlock decision lists all theses | tests/test_verdict.py |
| Garbage/index/empty elicitation answers never become constraints | tests/test_elicitor.py |
| Zhoda decision synthesized, not raw platform.answer | tests/test_verdict.py + tests/test_e2e.py |
| Birth unanimity fast-pass / DA spawn opposition | tests/test_e2e.py |
| Grounding gate: URL/deixis/empty object → insufficient_context, no debate | tests/test_e2e.py::test_url_answer_is_insufficient_context_and_skips_debate |
| Paraphrased elicitation questions asked once | tests/test_elicitor.py::test_paraphrased_questions_are_asked_once |
| One-option substring maps to that option | tests/test_elicitor.py::test_single_option_substring_counts_as_answer |
| --context files appear in position prompts | tests/test_e2e.py::test_context_files_land_in_position_prompt |
| Unasked elicitation → open_ambiguities, never assumptions | tests/test_elicitor.py + tests/test_e2e.py::test_auto_clarify_grounding_is_insufficient_without_context |
| Synthetic opposition labeled in minority / tree | tests/test_verdict.py::test_synthetic_opposition_is_labeled_in_minority + tests/test_plan.py::test_synthetic_faction_is_labeled_on_the_tree |
| Rotating DA skipped when synthetic opposition exists | tests/test_e2e.py::test_advocate_spawns_opposition_on_unanimous_debate |
| SOURCE: parsed into rebuttal_evidence_url | tests/test_debate.py::test_source_line_becomes_rebuttal_evidence_url |
| String "null" evidence_url → None / assumption | tests/test_plan.py::test_three_evidence_labels |
| Cost after all LLM; sum(breakdown)==requests; latency_s | tests/test_openrouter.py::test_latency_s_is_measured + tests/test_e2e.py::test_mixed_elicitation_answers_stay_honest |
| Elicitation answers reach positions/verdict; cache is answer-aware | tests/test_e2e.py::test_elicitation_answers_reach_positions_and_verdict |

When you add a mechanic to a docstring or docs/, add its test first or in the
same commit. When you change a schema, update docs/01-core.md in the same
commit (rule 10-python-core).
